From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:13:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/efi/capsules: No full flash access on S3 resume

enable_capsule_smi() runs on S3 resume too, so that the firmware
decides before the OS does (the payload does not run there), and it
decides with the boot mode in CBMEM. CBMEM is recovered on resume, not
rebuilt, and the boot mode is the one of the boot the OS resumes from:
FLASH_UPDATE when that boot had capsules, or OsIndications set. When
the payload found nothing to apply and gave the access up with
USE_FULL_FLASH (0), the resume would turn it on again, for the OS.

Today the lock of the vboot slot switch, also at BS_OS_RESUME, runs
first and seals the decision as "no capsules", by the order the
drivers link in. Do not rely on it: on S3 resume there are no capsules.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/drivers/efi/capsules.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/efi/capsules.c b/src/drivers/efi/capsules.c
index 8b02b636e3..356ee242b2 100644
--- a/src/drivers/efi/capsules.c
+++ b/src/drivers/efi/capsules.c
@@ -849,7 +849,12 @@ BOOT_STATE_INIT_ENTRY(BS_DEV_INIT, BS_ON_EXIT, parse_capsules, NULL);
 static void enable_capsule_smi(void *unused)
 {
 	uint32_t ret;
-	const bool supported = get_boot_mode() == LB_BOOT_MODE_FLASH_UPDATE;
+	/*
+	 * Never on S3 resume: the boot mode in CBMEM is the one of the boot
+	 * that the OS resumes from, and that one is over with its capsules.
+	 */
+	const bool supported = !acpi_is_wakeup_s3() &&
+			       get_boot_mode() == LB_BOOT_MODE_FLASH_UPDATE;
 	ret = call_smm(APM_CNT_SMMSTORE, SMMSTORE_CMD_USE_FULL_FLASH,
 		       (void *)(uintptr_t)supported);
 
